  "generated_text": "To determine what percent of the rectangle is shaded, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Define the dimensions of the rectangle:**\n   Let the width of the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) be \\(w\\). Since the rectangle is four times as long as it is wide, the length of the rectangle is \\(4w\\).\n\n2. **Identify the coordinates of the points:**\n   Place the rectangle in the coordinate plane with \\(A\\) at \\((0, w)\\), \\(B\\) at \\((0, 0)\\), \\(C\\) at \\((4w, 0)\\), and \\(D\\) at \\((4w, w)\\). Point \\(E\\) is the midpoint of \\(\\overline{BC}\\), so its coordinates are \\((2w, 0)\\).\n\n3. **Determine the area of the rectangle:**\n   The area of the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } ABCD = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} = 4w \\times w = 4w^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Identify the shaded regions:**\n   There are two gray triangles within the rectangle. The first gray triangle has vertices at \\(A\\), \\(E\\), and \\(C\\). The second gray triangle has vertices at \\(D\\), \\(E\\), and \\(B\\).\n\n5. **Calculate the area of the first gray triangle:**\n   The base of the triangle \\(AEC\\) is \\(2w\\) (the distance from \\(A\\) to \\(E\\)), and the height is \\(w\\) (the distance from \\(E\\) to the x-axis). The area of triangle \\(AEC\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } \\triangle AEC = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2w \\times w = w^2\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the area of the second gray triangle:**\n   The base of the triangle \\(DEB\\) is \\(2w\\) (the distance from \\(D\\) to \\(E\\)), and the height is \\(w\\) (the distance from \\(E\\) to the x-axis). The area of triangle \\(DEB\\) is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of } \\triangle DEB = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2w \\times w = w^2\n   \\]\n\n7. **Calculate the total shaded area:**\n   The total shaded area is the sum of the areas of the two gray triangles:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total shaded area} = w^2 + w^2 = 2w^2\n   \\]\n\n8. **Determine the percentage of the rectangle that is shaded:**\n   The percentage of the rectangle that is shaded is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage shaded} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Total shaded area}}{\\text{Area of } ABCD} \\right) \\times 100\\% = \\left( \\frac{2w^2}{4w^2} \\right) \\times 100\\% = \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\times 100\\% = 50\\%\n   \\]\n\nThus, the percentage of the rectangle that is shaded is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).",
